{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"e63f3ef3-751e-4fc0-ad7e-22a14b8bae2f","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause of the 500 error and the fix have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-jcO8uq/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n\n- **Cause**: On the initial publish to an empty table, `existing` was empty, so `similar` was `[]`. On subsequent publishes, `related()` computed similarity scores via `similarity()`, which returned Python `float` values. Boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects Python floats (`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead`), causing unhandled exceptions resulting in HTTP 500.\n- **Fix**:\n  - In [`src/app.py`](file:///tmp/h-jcO8uq/src/app.py#L22-L30), converted the score in `similarity()` to a `decimal.Decimal` via `Decimal(str(round(...)))`.\n  - In [`tests/test_publish.py`](file:///tmp/h-jcO8uq/tests/test_publish.py#L25-L42), added a regression test `test_publish_second_story_succeeds_with_similarity` to ensure publishing subsequent stories with related similarity scores succeeds.\n","duration_seconds":55.637299,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":190893,"output_tokens":2560,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":14508,"total_tokens":193453}}}
